{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "design": "Coverage-based test selection, design v37 (29 Oct 2026)",
  "scheme": "Shop",
  "platform": "ios",
  "default_branch": "main",
  "hash_stage": "Measured on the generated variant with `tuist hash selective-testing` (Tuist 4.216.0-canary.27): each scenario's hash.skipped lists the test targets whose hash equals the one its last passing run stored. The xcodeproj variant is expected to match except where a scenario overrides it; step 7 confirms it.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Target-level evidence is what a module's test processes executed outside every test- and suite-scoped record: a hosted app's launch, and the bodies of Swift Testing tests, which record no test scope. coverage_files' target rows hold the whole process today, so the rules must subtract the test and suite scopes; otherwise every XCTest test in a module whose target evidence includes a changed file is selected, and skips such as MoneyTests in source_change become selections.",
    "Target-level evidence counts as baseline evidence for owned_without_evidence, so a file that only Swift Testing tests executed is evidenced (swift_testing_only_source).",
    "matched_path is set for test_file_changed (the changed test file) and impacted (the first changed path in path order that the newest version or the module's target evidence includes), and absent for other reasons.",
    "The fallbacks that make the checkout a baseline (no_baseline, baseline_too_old, diff_too_large, excluded_branch) run every test without pruning by hash; hash.skipped is null for them.",
    "A full run with failing tests is still a baseline (failed_at_baseline).",
    "affected_modules lists the test modules that depend, directly or not, on the file's owning target, including the owner when it's a test target. A UI test target depends on its target application. Project-level files such as xcconfigs have no affected_modules.",
    "Each scenario is evaluated against its own fresh project and cache, with only its runs recorded before the checkout."
  ],
  "test_targets": {
    "CoreTests": {
      "framework": "xctest",
      "tests": [
        "MoneyTests/testFormatsDollars",
        "MoneyTests/testAddsAmounts",
        "DiscountTests/testTenPercentOff",
        "DiscountTests/testZeroPercentKeepsPrice"
      ]
    },
    "CatalogTests": {
      "framework": "mixed",
      "tests": [
        "CatalogLoadingTests/testBundledProductCount",
        "CatalogLoadingTests/testLookupBySKU",
        "CatalogFixtureTests/testFixtureParses",
        "SearchTests/matchesName()",
        "SearchTests/matchingIgnoresCase()"
      ]
    },
    "AppTests": {
      "framework": "swift_testing",
      "host": "App",
      "tests": [
        "CartTests/totalSumsItems()",
        "CartTests/discountAppliesToTotal()"
      ]
    },
    "AppUITests": {
      "framework": "xcuitest",
      "target_application": "App",
      "tests": [
        "ShopUITests/testShowsCatalog",
        "ShopUITests/testApplyingDiscountUpdatesTotal"
      ]
    }
  },
  "baseline_evidence": {
    "tests": {
      "CoreTests/MoneyTests/testFormatsDollars": [
        "Core/Sources/Money.swift",
        "CoreTests/MoneyTests.swift"
      ],
      "CoreTests/MoneyTests/testAddsAmounts": [
